-**Edge Cases and Pitfalls**
-*   **Coherence Dependency:** Interactive performance depends heavily on the coherence exhibited by secondary ray packets [S1].
-*   **Performance Degradation:** The performance impact is sublinear in the number of shadow rays traced, but large packets (e.g., $8 \times 8$) can significantly reduce frame rates [S1].
-*   **Light Size:** The light source area is fixed at 5% of the solid angle subtended by the scene bounding box for the tested configurations [S1].
+## Operating characteristics
+**Time and Memory Complexity:**
+- **Time Complexity:** The traversal time for a packet of $N \times N$ rays is sublinear in $N$ due to coherence, but still increases with packet size [S2]. The base traversal cost is determined by the modified CGT algorithm [S1].
+- **Memory Complexity:** Depends on the grid structure and particle storage, similar to primary ray casting [S1]. No additional significant memory is required for the shadow rays themselves beyond the packet storage [S2].
 
